  "title": "SC Orders Oversight by AG, SG in BCI Policy Decisions Ahead of Polls",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court of India ordered the Bar Council of India (BCI) to have oversight by the Attorney General for India and the Solicitor General for India, pending the reconstitution of the BCI chairperson Manan Kumar Mishra. The court emphasized the need for consultation with these officials before making policy decisions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court ordered the Bar Council of India (BCI) to have oversight by the Attorney General for India and the Solicitor General for India.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manan Kumar Mishra was first elected as BCI chairman until 2012, and he returned as chairman in November 2014.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The BCI chairperson's tenure was challenged by advocates in protest.",
      "confidence": 0.95
