    {
      "title": "SC asks AG, SG to join BCI policy decisions until body is reconstituted",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/sc-asks-ag-sg-to-join-bci-policy-decisions-until-body-is-reconstituted-126090201341_1.html",
      "description": "Supreme Court says it is not approving Manan Kumar Mishra's continuation as BCI chairman; State Bar Councils told to elect representatives within two weeks",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-02T13:56:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "BCI must consult AG, Solicitor General before taking policy decisions: SC",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/bci-must-consult-ag-solicitor-general-before-taking-policy-decisions-sc-126090200508_1.html",
      "description": "The Supreme Court on Wednesday said the Bar Council of India (BCI) has to take any policy decision in consultation with the Attorney General for India and the Solicitor General.\nThe top court was hearing pleas challenging the legality of Bar Council of India (BCI) chairperson Manan Kumar Mishra's prolonged tenure and seeking his removal from the post.\nA bench comprising Chief Justice Surya Kant and Justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohana was hearing the pleas.\n\"Both the Attorney General for India and the Solicitor General for India shall be actively associated with every policy decision taken by the Bar Council of India,\" the bench said.\nMishra was first elected as BCI chairman till 2012. Although Mishra briefly demitted office in 2014, he returned as chairman in November that year and has remained in the post since then, the plea filed by advocate Yogamaya MG said.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-02T07:44:47"
    }
  ]
